1
00:00:00,485 --> 00:00:06,010
Costco has sold the same hot dog
and soda for $1.50 since 1984.

2
00:00:06,030 --> 00:00:09,130
Prices everywhere else
have tripled since then.

3
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:11,074
The hot dog never moved.

4
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:16,072
In 2013, the CEO asked the founder
if he could finally raise it.

5
00:00:16,092 --> 00:00:20,844
The answer: If you raise the
effing hot dog, I will kill you.

6
00:00:20,864 --> 00:00:24,524
Costco says it makes little
or nothing on its food court.

7
00:00:24,564 --> 00:00:29,156
So how does a store that barely
profits on food make billions?

8
00:00:29,176 --> 00:00:34,196
Last year, Costco made $10.4
billion in operating profit.

9
00:00:34,216 --> 00:00:37,875
$5.3 billion of it came from one thing.

10
00:00:37,895 --> 00:00:43,305
Membership fees. And about nine in
ten members renew, every single year.

11
00:00:43,325 --> 00:00:47,228
The hot dog isn't the product.
It's the reason you come back.

12
00:00:47,248 --> 00:00:50,858
So enjoy the hot dog.
It's already paid for.
